  "description": "KAFXUM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C49 H111 Eu3 K3 O15 Ti1. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.600-3.621 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.22-99.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu3K3TiO2(OBut)11(OMe/OH)(HOBut).",
